.TH H07P-SETUP 8 "October 2026" "H07P" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
h07p-setup \- install and maintain the H07P dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B h07p-setup
.RI [ action ] " [package.deb] [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments, opens an interactive maintenance menu.
Install and update simulate dependency resolution before applying changes.
Unrelated package removals are rejected. Existing owner configuration is retained.
Mutations require root; diagnostics and dry runs can run without root.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B doctor
Show dependency, service and disk status without reading credentials or log contents.
.TP
.BR install ", " update
Install a trusted local H07P Debian package, resolving dependencies through APT.
Place its matching SHA256 file beside the package when available.
.TP
.B repair
Reinstall the most recently cached H07P package. A package path may be supplied.
.TP
.B rollback
Restore the previous protected release/configuration snapshot.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove H07P while retaining NAS, state, native accounts, authentication and backups.
.TP
.B refresh-index
Refresh existing APT repository indexes without upgrading installed packages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show the plan without installing, stopping services or modifying data.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Accept the displayed action without an interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit structured diagnostic or installation-plan output.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/cache/huou07-playground
Verified local package cache for repair.
.TP
.I /var/backups/huou07-playground
Root-private release and state snapshots.
.SH NOTES
Do not delete dpkg locks or credential files to repair a dependency conflict.
Use doctor, resolve the reported repository/network issue, then retry repair.
Native harness login and provider configuration remain unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
